Keep a tooltip away after a press on its element

A press hides an element's tooltip, but the delay to show it starts
over at the release, so it comes back over whatever the press opened —
a menu, a dialog, the view it switched to. Put it away at a press on the
element until the pointer leaves the element. The press itself then
keeps the tooltip from showing while the button is held, which the
hover checks no longer need to.

